  "content": {
    "id": "p44-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "$$(1+x)^n={}^nC_0+{}^nC_1x+\\cdots+{}^nC_nx^n\\qquad\\text{for }n\\geq1.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p44-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Differentiate both sides of the binomial expansion above.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$n(1+x)^{n-1}=\\displaystyle\\sum_{r=1}^{n}r\\,{}^nC_r x^{r-1}$.",
          "worked": "Treat $n$ and the binomial coefficients as constants:\n$$\\begin{aligned}n(1+x)^{n-1}&=\\sum_{r=1}^{n}r\\,{}^nC_r x^{r-1}\\\\&={}^nC_1+2{}^nC_2x+3{}^nC_3x^2+\\cdots+n{}^nC_nx^{n-1}.\\end{aligned}$$\nThe finite sum ends at $r=n$; when $n=1$, it contains only the first term.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "By substituting $x=1$, show that $1\\times{}^nC_1+2\\times{}^nC_2+\\cdots+n\\times{}^nC_n=n2^{n-1}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle\\sum_{r=1}^{n}r\\,{}^nC_r=n2^{n-1}$.",
          "worked": "Substitute $x=1$ into the differentiated identity:\n$$\\begin{aligned}n(1+1)^{n-1}&=\\sum_{r=1}^{n}r\\,{}^nC_r(1)^{r-1}\\\\n2^{n-1}&={}^nC_1+2{}^nC_2+\\cdots+n{}^nC_n.\\end{aligned}$$\nThe sum of each coefficient multiplied by its exponent index is the row index times half the sum of the whole row.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "For $n\\geq2$, by substituting $x=-1$, show that $1\\times{}^nC_1-2\\times{}^nC_2+\\cdots+(-1)^{n-1}n\\times{}^nC_n=0$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "For $n\\geq2$, $\\displaystyle\\sum_{r=1}^{n}(-1)^{r-1}r\\,{}^nC_r=0$.",
          "worked": "Substitute $x=-1$ into the differentiated identity:\n$$\\begin{aligned}n(1-1)^{n-1}&=\\sum_{r=1}^{n}r\\,{}^nC_r(-1)^{r-1}\\\\n(0)^{n-1}&={}^nC_1-2{}^nC_2+3{}^nC_3-\\cdots+(-1)^{n-1}n{}^nC_n\\\\0&={}^nC_1-2{}^nC_2+\\cdots+(-1)^{n-1}n{}^nC_n.\\end{aligned}$$\nSince $n\\geq2$, the exponent $n-1$ is positive. Thus the alternating sum of each coefficient multiplied by its exponent index is zero.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      }
    ]
  },
